// The swarm baseline: small, numerous, and cheap enough that the threat
// budget always affords a few. One bite barely registers — the lesson
// is that darts run out, not that any single skitter hurts
// (`SYSTEMS.md` §2.2, "ammo drain economics").
//
// No `min_provocation`: this is the one creature present from the very
// first wave, regardless of how the run has been played so far.
#![enable(implicit_some)]
EnemyDef(
    id: "enemy.skitter",
    name: "Skitter",
    glyph: "🐜",
    hp: 30,
    // Quick over open ground, but still slower than the tower's own
    // stride (60). These are not rushing you — you are walking into
    // where they live.
    speed_paces_per_100_ticks: 40,
    damage: 4,
    attack_ticks: 25,
    // Ten seconds of chewing at 4 damage every 25 ticks — 48 hit
    // points. The four skitters an opening wave fields do 192 between
    // them: an unanswered wave costs a panel (150) and starts on
    // whatever is behind it. A scrape, as intended, rather than the
    // 576 the first pass at this number produced.
    cling_ticks: 300,
    approach: Ground,
    // Five threat, and the cheapest thing in the pack — which makes it
    // the creature that decides when a wave can happen at all, since
    // nothing comes until the provocation-scaled budget can afford the
    // cheapest eligible creature on its own. At
    // `threat_per_100_provocation` 40 that puts the earliest possible
    // wave at provocation 13. `base_threat` (`balance.ron`, 10) then
    // buys two of them, so the first wave a run sees is a pair of
    // skitters and nothing worse. See BALANCE.md.
    threat: 5,
)
